WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Most people think if you want to start a

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:06.680
real business that you need a building,

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:08.440
a storefront, a lease, a gym venue, or

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.520
something with four walls and a rent

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.480
payment every single month. But, some of

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.840
the most interesting businesses that I

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.280
found don't have any of that. They have

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.200
a trailer. They hook it up, they drive

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.760
it to the customer, and they get paid

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.600
when they get there. So, today I'm

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.680
breaking down these seven businesses

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.520
that you can run out of a trailer, what

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.760
they charge, what it costs you to get it

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.680
going, and what the numbers can actually

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.720
look like for you. And my name's Austin

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.720
Zaback. I've built multiple businesses

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.520
over the last decade primarily in real

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.320
estate, pest control, and a handful of

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.160
other industries. And if you get any

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.960
value out of today's video, do me a huge

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.960
favor. Just smash that like button for

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.680
the YouTube algorithm, and subscribe if

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.120
you haven't already. Okay, so let's go

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.520
ahead and start one that takes a

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.720
business that usually needs a huge

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.720
building, and it puts it on wheels. And

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:57.280
that is a fitness trailer. Daniel Prawl

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.480
runs Level Up Mobile Gym in Miami. And

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.760
instead of signing a lease on a gym, he

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:04.640
pulls a trailer loaded with equipment

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.800
out to parks and outdoor spots. He opens

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.800
the trailer up and runs group fitness

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.600
classes right there. The company has

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.600
advertised more than 220 clients, and

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.840
they did it with one coach and one

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.480
trailer. Now, think about how different

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.320
this is from a normal gym. A normal gym

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.560
has rent, utilities, and a giant space

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.280
that sits empty for half of the day.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.840
You're paying for that space whether

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.200
anybody shows up or not. Here, the gym

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.360
shows up where people already are. And a

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.400
lot of people would honestly rather work

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.280
out of a park than in a crowded building

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.480
anyways. And because these are small

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.320
group classes, the math works in your

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.520
favor. If you're a personal trainer,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.000
you're trading 1 hour for one client.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.600
Here, one coach is getting paid by a

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.880
whole group of people in that same hour.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.160
So, let's just talk about numbers a

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.960
little bit. Level Up recently ran an

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:58.120
8-week promotion, which is 24 classes

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:00.320
for $299, or unlimited classes for $449.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:03.040
So, let's just use the $299 package for

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:05.880
example. If you got 50 people to buy it,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:09.280
that would be $14,950

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.840
over 8 weeks, or about $7,500 every 4

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.680
weeks. And if some of these people

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.959
upgraded to the unlimited at $449, that

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.120
number would go up without you adding a

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:19.920
single extra coach. Now, here's where

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.040
the real money is. When those 8 weeks

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.160
are up, the people who liked it will buy

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.800
it again. So, you're not finding 50

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.440
brand new customers every couple of

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.240
months. You're keeping the ones that you

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.240
already have, and then you're adding to

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.040
them. Now, to get started here, you are

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.680
going to be looking at somewhere around

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.760
$40,000

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.680
okay? And that'll cover the training

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:41.000
trailer, all the equipment, and some

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.920
money to get launched. Now, the best way

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.480
to fill your first class is to go where

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.560
customers already are. Pick a park, pick

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.000
a consistent time, and show up there

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.760
every single week. People walking by see

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.760
a group working out, they see the

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.280
trailer, and that right there is your

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.160
marketing. And when you're ready to

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.080
grow, you don't need a bigger building.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.959
You just add another location, you add

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.920
another time slot. Okay, the next one on

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.959
today's list is basically every kid's

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.560
dream birthday party, and that is a

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:09.360
mobile gaming and VR trailer. So,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.680
ReadyUp Mobile Gaming in Northern

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:14.040
Kentucky pulls a climate control trailer

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.360
full of video games and VR into

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.280
somebody's driveway. So, all of the kids

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.400
get to just walk outside, and there's a

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:22.080
full gaming setup waiting for them. And

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.680
because it's climate controlled, it

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.680
doesn't matter if it's in the middle of

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.440
summer or in the middle of winter. Now,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.920
think about who's actually paying here.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.040
It's not the kid, it's the parents. And

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.959
the parent is usually the one stressed

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.800
out about the party. Where do we have

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:37.320
the party? How do we keep all these kids

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.600
entertained? And who's going to be

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.320
cleaning up afterwards? Now, if you take

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.720
them to an arcade, you're driving

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.680
everybody there, and you're trying to

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.400
keep track of them the entire time. But

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.519
with this, somebody pulls up to the

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.600
house, the kids are entertained for 2

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:52.440
hours, and then the trailer leaves. And

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.560
that's what the parent is really buying.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.560
They're buying a party that is basically

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:59.440
handled for them. Ready Up charges $400

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.560
